e7 wire log v1
device   GS Music e7, serial 361, USB, driven from Node over CoreMIDI
input    GS-e7 Analog Synthesizer
output   GS-e7 Analog Synthesizer
date     2026-08-19
session  Reading preset 1.1.1 a block at a time, one send per block, watching for the preview frame of protocol-quirks.md #12

# Every Read Memory here drew exactly one frame, and every frame is a 34-byte
# spec-shaped memory-data response: no preview frame, no malformed frame, nothing
# short. This is the normal case, and the reason protocol-quirks.md #12 no longer
# claims the device sends a prelude.
#
# Answers lag their command by one on this path (HW-11), so a frame sits under the
# command after the one it answers, and the frame at +0.0ms answers a warm-up read
# taken before the log was cleared. The first two frames both carry "Pumpin Pad",
# which is block 0 read twice. The lag belongs to this transport rather than to the
# instrument; nothing here pairs a frame with the line above it.
